assertion  XSH.iswspace.001
anchor     functions/iswspace.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswspace.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswspace() returns non-zero for each character
           of the class space as the locale definition lists it: the space,
           form feed, newline, carriage return, tab and vertical tab.
test       t/001-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswspace.002
anchor     functions/iswspace.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswspace.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswspace() returns 0 for each of these
           characters, which the locale definition does not place in the
           class: the letters, the digits, the punctuation and the controls
           other than those five.
test       t/002-non-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswspace.003
anchor     functions/iswspace.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswspace.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       iswspace(WEOF) is within the domain and returns 0, since WEOF is
           not a character of the class.
test       t/003-weof.c

assertion  XSH.iswspace.004
anchor     functions/iswspace.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswspace.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       None of the six white-space characters is alpha, digit, xdigit,
           punct or graph.
test       t/004-space-relations.c

assertion  XSH.iswspace.005
anchor     functions/iswspace.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswspace.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In a UTF-8 locale, iswspace() is still non-zero for the six
           white-space characters.
note       Needs an installed multibyte UTF-8 locale (NOTINUSE otherwise);
           only ASCII-range characters are examined.
test       t/005-utf8-portable.c
